/// target group, use the State element in the response. When you attach a
/// target group to an Auto Scaling group, the initial State value is Adding
/// . The state transitions to Added after all Auto Scaling instances are
/// registered with the target group. If Elastic Load Balancing health
/// checks are enabled for the Auto Scaling group, the state transitions to
/// InService after at least one Auto Scaling instance passes the health
/// check. When the target group is in the InService state, Amazon EC2 Auto
/// Scaling can terminate and replace any instances that are reported as
/// unhealthy. If no registered instances pass the health checks, the target
/// group doesn't enter the InService state. Target groups also have an
/// InService state if you attach them in the CreateAutoScalingGroup API
/// call. If your target group state is InService , but it is not working
